, carries no visible dependency edge, and no such 'identity fallback' / 'conditional identity' guidance is locatable in either skill file or the repo — so the relied-upon functionality cannot be confirmed and fails closed.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe6afdea9c14a5a11","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan bullet 1 ('Make the implementation skill use atomic `rebar claim` with the conditional identity guidance established by F15') and AC line 2 ('uses the F15 identity fallback and does not prescribe a bare handle')","norm_id":"nf3929651f2d62288","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Author implements the skill edit and must supply the exact F15 identity-fallback wording, but the plan never states what it is and no prerequisite artifact establishes it — the AC becomes unsatisfiable as written or gets filled with an invented mechanism."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Inline the concrete conditional-identity fallback wording the implementation skill must adopt (default_assignee applies identity; empty leaves it unassigned; `--assignee` only for explicit override), or cite it in resolvable form (e.g. `templates/rebar-usage.md` / `templates/AGENTS.md`), instead of referring to 'the F15 identity fallback'.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan quote: 'Make the implementation skill use atomic `rebar claim` with the conditional identity guidance established by F15.'","AC quote: 'The implementation skill uses the F15 identity fallback and does not prescribe a bare handle.'","search_files for 'F15' returns no ticket/alias/doc in the repo — only a prior plan-review cache entry that itself flagged: 'Cite F15 in resolvable [rebar:<id>] form (or inline the concrete conditional-identity fallback wording the skill must adopt)'.","The concrete rule exists at templates/rebar-usage.md:22 and templates/AGENTS.md:46 ('When ticket.default_assignee is configured, claim applies that identity. When the setting is empty, the claimed ticket remains unassigned. Pass --assignee only for an explicit override.') but the plan never points to that source.","T8 checklist (b): a processing protocol/decision rule referenced but not co-located with the schema/surface that needs it."],"finding":"The plan tells the implementation skill to adopt 'the F15 identity fallback' / 'the conditional identity guidance established by F15', but F15 is a plan label (not a resolvable citation), and the concrete fallback wording the skill must write is never co-located or inlined in the plan. An executor cannot determine what identity-fallback prose to author from the plan text alone.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb78d9ef37d5912ea","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'Plan' bullet 1 and Acceptance Criteria line 2 ('uses the F15 identity fallback and does not prescribe a bare handle')","norm_id":"n26ad237b6b81c284","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An executor rewrites rebar-implement/SKILL.md's Phase 2/Phase 3 claim commands but, lacking the F15 wording, invents a fallback that still prescribes a bare `--assignee <you>` handle — violating AC line 2.","A plan reviewer cannot verify AC line 2 because 'the F15 identity fallback' has no in-plan definition to check against."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Replace 'the conditional identity guidance established by F15' with the concrete rule and a resolvable source: 'the conditional-identity guidance in templates/rebar-usage.md / templates/AGENTS.md — `rebar claim <id>` with no `--assignee` (default_assignee applies identity when configured, otherwise the ticket stays unassigned); pass `--assignee` only for an explicit override; never prescribe a bare handle.'","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add an acceptance criterion asserting that the implementa